/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 429 0 R
/T (PingCastle explains that without the "This account is sensitive and cannot be delegated" flag, an administrator account can be impersonated through Kerberos delegation by a compromised service account. The recommended mitigation is to enable this flag or add privileged accounts to the built-in Protected Users group. The recommendation references STIG V-36435 and the MITRE ATT&CK framework \(Active Directory Configuration mitigation\).)
/E (PingCastle explains that without the "This account is sensitive and cannot be delegated" flag, an administrator account can be impersonated through Kerberos delegation by a compromised service account. The recommended mitigation is to enable this flag or add privileged accounts to the built-in Protected Users group. The recommendation references STIG V-36435 and the MITRE ATT&CK framework \(Active Directory Configuration mitigation\).)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
