<<
/Title (PingCastle explains that if an account configured with unconstrained delegation exists and the Print Spooler service is running on the domain controller, an attacker can force the domain controller to authenticate to an attacker-controlled machine, capture its Kerberos Ticket Granting Ticket \(TGT\), and subsequently perform a DCSync attack to extract every password hash stored in Active Directory, ultimately impersonating any domain account, including the Domain Administrator.)
/Dest [37 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
